From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: 3DS cheats: a folder shared with the standalone Azahar, RetroArch's menu

Adapted for ROCKNIX: the paths below are ROCKNIX's, not dArkOS's.

retro_cheat_reset and retro_cheat_set did nothing, so RetroArch's cheats
never reached the core. Now (shared_cheats.cpp):

- The cheats live in /storage/.config/azahar/cheats, the standalone
  Azahar's cheats folder, laid out as GammaOS's azahar-nano keeps them
  (CheatDb, GammaOSNextDistribution-14 dbb613ef825): <TID>.txt is every
  cheat of a title with its *citra_enabled mark, custom/<TID>.txt the
  user's own. The core's cheats folder points there, so its cheat engine
  loads the list at boot and saves the marks to it.
- Before a game boots the list is rebuilt: the user's own cheats, then the
  database's (/usr/share/azahar/cheats3ds, one <TID>.txt per title, if
  present), the marks carried over by name and code, then by name; cheats
  of the list in neither source are kept as the user's own.
- RetroArch gets the same list as the game's cheat file
  (/tmp/database/cht/Azahar/<content>.cht), which it reads right after
  retro_load_game, for Quick Menu > Cheats. Applying cheats there is a
  reset and one set per enabled cheat, counted among the enabled ones, so
  each is found in the engine by its code and switched; a code typed into
  RetroArch becomes one of the user's own ("RetroArch code N"). The marks
  are saved at the next frame and when the game closes.

A user's cheat that the database has too (same name and code) is listed
once, where the database has it.

AZAHAR_CHEATS_DIR, AZAHAR_CHEAT_DB and AZAHAR_RA_CHEATS_DIR override the
three paths.

